  "codingDoctrine": {
    "fixAssessment": "Root cause: after every host publish both wake-time consumers started from nothing: the grant projection paged the host log from revision 0 through an adapter that re-read the whole host log on every 500-row page, and assigned sequences to every visible identity; the replica ingest re-read, re-parsed and re-folded its whole stream. Fix: the grant session keeps the position its last page stopped at and the projection reads, filters and assigns only the rows after it; the adapter passes the page start to getCampaignEvents(fromSequence); the replica store keeps, per stream, the last revision read and the fold through it and reads only the rows after it.",
    "removed": [
      "a per-guest map on the registry entry or a module map keyed by grant: the session owns the cursor and serializes its projections",
      "a public position type carrying the stream revision: campaignDelivery.boundary.test.ts forbids journal positions on the public result types, so the page carries an opaque token and projectCampaignStreamForGrant keeps what it stands for in a module-private WeakMap",
      "a new journal method or head port (src/lib/events stays untouched)",
      "caching the replica envelope list: the fold (apply state and identities) is kept instead",
      "an incremental record rewrite: the record is lossy and the step is flat by the rule (see the timing table)"
    ],
    "scope": "8 product files: hostCampaignEventJournal.ts, handleRoomCodeGuestJoin.ts, projectCampaignStreamForGrant.ts, campaignDeliveryTypes.ts, campaignGrantChannelSession.ts, SQLiteCampaignReplicaStore.ts, planCampaignReplicaIngest.ts, campaignReplicaEnvelope.ts. The token grant join (handleCampaignGrantJoin.ts) uses the same session class and so also keeps a position; callers that pass none (snapshot build, equivalence verifier) keep the full read.",
    "designChangeAfterAdmission": "The admission receipt described the position as a public object {deliveryEpochId, afterRevision, withheld} on the page. The first focused run failed campaignDelivery.boundary.test.ts (\"does not declare streamRevision or commitPosition on public types\"; its regex matched the expression `?.streamRevision ??` in projectCampaignStreamForGrant.ts, and its stated contract is that journal positions stay off the public result types). The position became an opaque branded token (campaignDeliveryTypes.ts) resolved through a module-private WeakMap in projectCampaignStreamForGrant.ts; the boundary test was not changed."
  },
